---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { downgrades, KIND_LABEL, priorIncidents } from "../lib/data.js";
const rows = downgrades();
const prior = priorIncidents();
---
<Base title="Downgrades" current="downgrades"
      description="Devices that lost function after people had already bought them.">
  <h1>Downgrades</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Devices that got <strong>worse after people had already bought them</strong> — a
    firmware update that added an account requirement, a server shutdown, a feature moved
    behind a subscription, a vendor revoking access it had previously granted.
  </p>
  <p class="lede">
    This is the page the whole project exists to fill, and it is deliberately kept narrow.
    Routine additions to the catalog live on <a href="/updates/">Updates</a> so that
    anything appearing here is worth your attention.
  </p>
  <h2>Since we started watching</h2>
  {rows.length === 0 ? (
    <p class="empty">
      Nothing yet. No device we list has lost function since we verified it. That is the
      outcome we want — but read it precisely: this catalogue is young, and an empty
      section here means little has had time to change, not that we have proved nothing did.
    </p>
  ) : (
    <div class="tablewrap">
    <table class="devices">
      <tbody>
        {rows.map((c) => (
          <tr>
            <td class="num">{c.date}</td>
            <td><span class={`kind k-${c.kind}`}>{KIND_LABEL[c.kind]}</span></td>
            <td>
              <a href={c.device.status === "rejected" ? "/rejected/" : `/device/${c.device.model_id}/`}>
                {c.device.make} {c.device.model}
              </a>
            </td>
            <td>{c.change}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
  )}

  <h2>Before we started watching</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    These happened before this catalogue existed. We did not catch them — we recorded
    them, from public reporting — and they are kept separate so nothing here implies we
    were watching when we were not. They are on this page because they are precisely what
    it is about, and because the pattern is the reason to care about the rest of the site.
  </p>
  <div class="tablewrap">
  <table class="devices">
    <tbody>
      {prior.map((i) => (
        <tr>
          <td class="num">{i.date}</td>
          <td><a href={`/vendors/#${i.vendor.slug}`}>{i.vendor.name}</a></td>
          <td>
            {i.description}
            <br /><span class="evc">{i.class}</span> <a href={i.source} rel="nofollow">source</a>
          </td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
  <p class="age">
    Vendor conduct is scored in the <a href="/vendors/">ledger</a>, separately from any
    device's tier. A company that has done this before can do it again, but it does not
    change what the hardware in front of you does today.
  </p>
</Base>
